course: dictionary
lesson: 7260
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pigsty has two: a real pen on a farm where pigs are kept, and an informal word for a very dirty or untidy room or place. The words around it show you which one is meant.
explain: «The pigs rolled in the mud of the pigsty all afternoon.» The pigs and the farm tell you it means the animal pen. Now read «Your room is a pigsty!» A bedroom is not a farm, so the word must mean a mess. Parents are not saying your room has pigs in it.
explain: This is a metaphor: the word is used to describe something it does not literally mean. Check by swapping in the meaning: «Your room is a pen where pigs are kept» makes no sense, but «Your room is very messy» does. That tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Pigsty has two meanings: a pen or small building on a farm where pigs are kept, and an informal word for a very dirty or untidy room or place.
fact: In a story about a farm, «pigsty» usually means the real pen. In talk about bedrooms, it usually means a mess.
fact: «Muck out the pigsty» means to clean the dirt out of the pig pen.
fact: Saying «my room is a pigsty» compares a messy room to a pigsty, without meaning it literally.
fact: People call a messy room a pigsty, but pigs are among the cleanest and cleverest animals on the farm.
exercise: «The pigs rolled happily in the pigsty.» What is a pigsty here? | *A pen or small building on a farm where pigs are kept | A sleepy cat | A very tidy kitchen | A field of tall corn
exercise: Mum says, «Your room is a pigsty!» What does she mean? | Your room is very quiet | Your room has pigs living in it | *Your room is very messy | Your room is on a farm
exercise: Find and copy one word that means untidy: «People call a messy room a pigsty, but pigs are among the cleanest and cleverest animals on the farm.» | cleverest | farm | pigs | *messy
test: Dad leaned on the gate of the pigsty and counted the piglets. What does pigsty mean? | *A pen where pigs are kept | A very dirty room | A kind of hat | A small shop
test: «My bedroom looks like a pigsty today.» What does the phrase like a pigsty suggest? | It is freshly painted | It has been cleaned for guests | *It is very untidy | It smells of flowers
exam: Lena says, «Clean out the pigsty before lunch.» What does she want you to do? | To buy a new pig | To paint the farmhouse | *To clean the dirt out of the pig pen | To tidy your bedroom
